---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About · Stop the Slop"
  description="What this list is, how something earns a spot on it, and what the verdicts mean."
  current="about"
>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1 class="display">About<span style="color:var(--ink)">.</span></h1>
    <div class="prose-card">
      <p>
        Stop the Slop is a list of the stuff that actually helps you keep AI slop out of
        your work: tools that catch it, guides that teach you to see it, standards worth
        adopting, and the people covering the mess. Made by designers, for anyone who ships
        creative work.
      </p>

      <h2>How something earns a spot</h2>
      <p>
        A person here actually read it, ran it, or used it. Every entry gets a short
        honest note in plain language (never a rehash of the thing&rsquo;s own marketing),
        a verdict, and a checked date. Lists like this rot; the date is the promise that
        someone is still paying attention.
      </p>

      <h2>The verdicts</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>GO</strong> means it&rsquo;s good. Use it.<br />
        <strong>CAUTION</strong> means it&rsquo;s useful, with a catch we name in the note.<br />
        <strong>STOP</strong> means we tried it so you don&rsquo;t have to.
      </p>
      <p>
        No stars, no scores out of ten. Old-school product testers printed named verdicts
        and stood behind them; that&rsquo;s the whole system, and it fits in three words.
      </p>

      <h2>What doesn&rsquo;t get in</h2>
      <p>
        Detection theater and slop laundering. A few of the worst offenders are cataloged
        anyway, under <strong>STOP</strong>, because naming the failing product is a public
        service.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Something missing, dead, or wrong?
        <a href="https://github.com/laltaffer/stoptheslop/issues">Open an issue</a>.
        The whole list is a public repository; every entry is a file anyone can read and
        argue with.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
